  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 25,
    "summary": "David pleads for truth and asks for pardon—Mercy and truth are for those who keep the commandments.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Unto thee, O Lord, do I lift up my soul.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Ps. 86:4; 143:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O my God, I trust in thee: let me not be ashamed, let not mine enemies triumph over me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Faith; Trust in God."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Shame."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, let none that wait on thee be ashamed: let them be ashamed which transgress without cause.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Worthiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Shew me thy ways, O Lord; teach me thy paths.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Ex. 33:13 (12–13); Ps. 143:8 (5–12); John 14:6; D&C 50:17 (17–20); 76:2 (1–5); 79:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Lead me in thy truth, and teach me: for thou art the God of my salvation; on thee do I wait all the day.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "TG Guidance, Divine; Leadership."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Gen. 49:18; Prov. 20:22; Isa. 40:31; 2 Ne. 6:13 (7, 13)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Remember, O Lord, thy tender mercies and thy lovingkindnesses; for they have been ever of old.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG God, Mercy of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions: according to thy mercy remember thou me for thy goodness’ sake, O Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Job 13:26; D&C 20:5; 58:42; JS—H 1:28 (28–29)."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "Ps. 51:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Good and upright is the Lord: therefore will he teach sinners in the way.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "TG Education."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The meek will he guide in judgment: and the meek will he teach his way.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Guidance, Divine."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "All the paths of the Lord are mercy and truth unto such as keep his covenant and his testimonies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For thy name’s sake, O Lord, pardon mine iniquity; for it is great.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Ps. 109:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "What man is he that feareth the Lord? him shall he teach in the way that he shall choose.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "His soul shall dwell at ease; and his seed shall inherit the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Earth, Destiny of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The secret of the Lord is with them that fear him; and he will shew them his covenant.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Mysteries of Godliness."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Mine eyes are ever toward the Lord; for he shall pluck my feet out of the net.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "Ps. 141:8; D&C 4:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Ps. 9:15; 31:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Turn thee unto me, and have mercy upon me; for I am desolate and afflicted.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG God, Mercy of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The troubles of my heart are enlarged: O bring thou me out of my distresses.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Look upon mine affliction and my pain; and forgive all my sins.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Pain."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Consider mine enemies; for they are many; and they hate me with cruel hatred.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Cruelty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O keep my soul, and deliver me: let me not be ashamed; for I put my trust in thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "TG Shame."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Trust in God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let integrity and uprightness preserve me; for I wait on thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Redeem Israel, O God, out of all his troubles.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "Deut. 21:8; Ps. 130:8; D&C 84:99 (99–100)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
